prehistoric|before-written-history|ADJECTIVE|before written records|Belonging to a time before written records of history.|thuộc thời tiền sử|The museum displayed prehistoric tools found near the river.|Bảo tàng trưng bày những công cụ thời tiền sử được tìm thấy gần sông.|Usually before a noun; prehistoric people or tools. The relevant period varies between regions.|-
sew|join-with-thread|VERB|join with stitches|To join or attach material by making stitches with a needle and thread.|may; khâu|Grandmother sewed a new pocket onto my gardening apron.|Bà khâu thêm một chiếc túi mới vào tạp dề làm vườn của tôi.|Sew, sewed, sewn or sewed; sew something onto something. Sewing can be by hand or machine.|-
yellow|having-yellow-colour|ADJECTIVE|having the colour of a lemon|Having the bright colour commonly seen in a ripe lemon.|màu vàng|A yellow ribbon marked the path to the meeting place.|Một dải ruy băng màu vàng đánh dấu lối đến điểm hẹn.|Yellow can precede a noun or follow be; yellowish means somewhat yellow.|0
yellow|yellow-colour|NOUN|yellow as a colour|The colour commonly seen in a ripe lemon.|màu vàng|She added a little yellow to the green paint.|Cô thêm một ít màu vàng vào sơn màu xanh lá.|Usually uncountable for the colour; a yellow can refer to a particular shade.|1
double|two-part|ADJECTIVE|having two similar parts|Consisting of two similar parts or providing for two people.|đôi; có hai phần tương tự|The studio has a double door opening onto the courtyard.|Xưởng có một cửa hai cánh mở ra sân.|Usually before a noun: double door, double room. Exact meaning depends on the noun.|0
double|twice-quantity-before-noun|DETERMINER|twice the amount before a noun|Twice as much or as many as a stated or understood amount.|gấp đôi|The larger pot holds double the amount of water.|Chiếc nồi lớn chứa lượng nước gấp đôi.|Double the amount or double my salary; followed by a noun phrase identifying the quantity.|1
double|twice-quantity-alone|PRONOUN|twice an understood amount|An amount that is twice another amount already understood.|số lượng gấp đôi|The first box held twelve tools, and the second held double.|Hộp thứ nhất chứa mười hai dụng cụ, còn hộp thứ hai chứa gấp đôi.|Pronoun use stands without a following noun when the reference quantity is clear.|2
double|become-twice|VERB|become or make twice as much|To become twice as large, or make something twice as large.|tăng gấp đôi; làm tăng gấp đôi|The club doubled its membership after opening a weekend class.|Câu lạc bộ tăng gấp đôi số thành viên sau khi mở một lớp cuối tuần.|Transitive or intransitive: double the number, the number doubled. Doubled is regular.|3
double|pay-twice|ADVERB|at twice the amount|At twice the usual or stated amount.|gấp đôi|Visitors paid double during the special evening session.|Khách trả gấp đôi trong buổi đặc biệt vào tối đó.|Pay double, cost double; modifies the verb rather than a following noun.|4
etiquette|rules-of-politeness|NOUN|social rules of politeness|Accepted ways of behaving politely in a particular social setting.|phép lịch sự; nghi thức ứng xử|The guide explained dining etiquette before the formal meal.|Người hướng dẫn giải thích phép lịch sự khi ăn uống trước bữa ăn trang trọng.|Uncountable; dining etiquette, rules of etiquette. Expectations vary by setting and culture.|-
